examples.question_text:
Write $\underset{\sim}{v}$ in component notation. Each grid square represents $1$ unit.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\definecolor{gridcolour}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[step=7mm,draw=gridcolour,very thin] (0,0) grid (6,5);
\draw[-{Stealth},draw=black,line width=0.8pt] (5,4)--(1,1);
\path (3,2.5) node[above left] {$\underset{\sim}{v}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Read from tail to tip: $4$ units left and $3$ units down. Both components are negative.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\definecolor{gridcolour}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\definecolor{componentblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{componentred}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[step=7mm,draw=gridcolour,very thin] (0,0) grid (6,5);
\draw[-{Stealth},draw=componentblue,line width=0.8pt] (5,4)--(1,4);
\draw[-{Stealth},draw=componentred,line width=0.8pt] (1,4)--(1,1);
\draw[-{Stealth},draw=black,line width=0.8pt] (5,4)--(1,1);
\path (3,4) node[above] {$-4\underset{\sim}{i}$};
\path (1,2.5) node[left] {$-3\underset{\sim}{j}$};
\path (3,2.5) node[below right] {$\underset{\sim}{v}$};
\draw[draw=black,line width=0.4pt] (1.25,4)--(1.25,3.75)--(1,3.75);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\underset{\sim}{v}=-4\underset{\sim}{i}-3\underset{\sim}{j}$.
